 "brief": "# Build: ui-review-predicted (Urgent profile)\n\nBrett, Nov 3 2026 (voice): UI Review must show PREDICTED pictures - what a build will probably look like - BEFORE it's built, so he can approve the look before an agent spends money. Assigned agent: **Snap Sully** (book on his card; he's also on ui-review-shots - run after it or build on its storage fix; if the all-rounder router is on main and he's busy, whoever is free - record who). Register in Urgent (id `ui-review-predicted`) + banner entry. Mark the predicted-shots part of pending item `batch-manager` as moved here (pending_change note).\n\n## Build\n- s1 Predicted mockups: when a build is launched (or added to the orchestrator/pending list), generate a mockup per screen it will touch from the brief + step list (+ diff so far while running): render real framework components with the current theme/assets and demo data in a headless browser (reuse rebuild-shots / ui-screenshots capture tooling; do NOT build a new capture system). Phone + desktop. If an LLM is needed to turn the brief into a mockup spec, do it ONCE per build at launch with the cheapest capable model and cache it; record the cost on the item.\n- s2 UI Review item created at launch with status 'Predicted - approve the look', badge 'Predicted', before = current real screen (from main), after = predicted mockup. Brett can Approve look / Ask changes (comment goes to the build as an addendum before it starts or at the next step) / Reject (build is held, not started).\n- s3 Setting (Claude settings / UI Review settings): 'Wait for my look approval before UI builds start' (default OFF; when ON, UI-touching builds queue until the predicted look is approved).\n- s4 While running, the predicted shot refreshes as the diff grows; when the build finishes, the real after-shot replaces it live (badge 'Real'), with a toggle to compare predicted vs real.\n- s5 Backfill: create predicted items now for every queued/running build that touches UI (toolbar-tap-confirm, crew-live, follow-amber, claude-settings, agent-pick, home-cards-live, smart-menus).\n- s6 Commands declared once -> REST + MCP + CLI (predict, list predicted, approve look). Tests, screenshots, report `_claude/builds/reports/ui-review-predicted.md`, THREADS, PR, steps through the store. Commits clean and professional.",
